# packages/uikit — component kit

The rules of the root `AGENTS.md` apply. This file holds only local ones.

## Boundaries

- No internal dependencies at all. UIKit knows nothing about other packages in the repository or about the project domain.
- Membership test: if a component needs a domain type, a domain word, or business-logic state, it is not a UIKit component but part of a screen, and it belongs in the app.
- Granular exports, no barrel: `@{{ project_name }}/uikit/components/<name>`, `@{{ project_name }}/uikit/lib/utils`, `@{{ project_name }}/uikit/hooks/<name>`. This is the shadcn convention: `shadcn add` drops in a file, and it is importable right away without editing an index.

## Conventions

We follow shadcn: a component is copied into the repository and is ours. Configuration is `components.json`: style `base-nova`, component base `@base-ui/react`, base color `zinc`, icons `@remixicon/react`, Geist font, CSS variables. Components are added as needed (`bunx shadcn add <name>` from this directory); the template ships none, since every project has its own.

In short: variants via `cva` with explicit `defaultVariants`; classes are merged via `cn` from `lib/utils`; `className` is accepted and passed last; props extend the element's native type and are passed through via `...props`.

## Color

Only theme tokens from `src/styles/globals.css`. Literals `#rrggbb`, `rgb()`, `oklch()` and Tailwind color classes inside a component are forbidden: they break the dark theme. Need a new color? Add the token to both blocks at once, `:root` and `.dark`.

## Checks

`bun run --filter '@{{ project_name }}/uikit' typecheck`, `bun run --filter '@{{ project_name }}/uikit' test`, `bunx biome check packages/uikit`.
